In article <9007242339.AA11370@cie.uoregon.edu> ghudson@CIE.UOREGON.EDU writes:
>> I have a character sitting on the Medusa level with no
>> way I know of to blind myself.
>     I also am about to have this problem in a game.  I'm 
>considering an interesting solution: curse a unicorn 
>horn.  Requires an extra unicorn horn and some unholy 
>water, both of which aren't too tough to get, esp. for a 
>chaotic chracter.  I've found that applying a cursed 
>unicorn horn will blind, confuse, hallucinate, or stun 
>you; with a lot of fiddling around with cursed an 
>uncursed 'corn horns, one should be able to blind oneself.

It may also give you deadly food poisoning.  (So watch out, and be sure to
have an _un_cursed horn around to cure the food poisoning if you get it.)

Other solution: if you have stealth, you can go up to the medusa while it's
not awake, zap it with cancellation, and then kill it.  The trouble is that
there are things which will wake monsters up, such as stepping on a squeaky
board trap.
